cker</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Jaffrelot</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Predicting deep venous thrombosis in pregnancy: external validation of the LEFT clinical prediction rule</article-title><source>Haematologica</source><volume>98</volume><year>2013</year><fpage>545</fpage><lpage>548</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">23065510</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref10"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Le Moigne</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Genty</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Meunier</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnoult</surname><given-names>A.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Righini</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bressollette</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Validation of the LEFt score, a newly proposed diagnostic tool for deep vein thrombosis in pregnant women</article-title><source>Thromb Res</source><volume>134</volume><year>2014</year><fpage>664</fpage><lpage>667</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">25087889</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref11"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van der Pol</surname><given-names>L.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mairuhu</surname><given-names>A.T.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tromeur</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Couturaud</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Huisman</surname><given-names>M.V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Klok</surname><given-names>F.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of clinical prediction rules and D-dimer tests in the diagnostic management of pregnant patie